# CONTRACT: Per-machine OVERRIDES for `pnpm dev` only — copying this file is
# optional, and empty is the correct steady state. angular.json's ngxEnv.files
# reads ../../.env.local.web FIRST, which `make env-file` generates and the
# container builds from, so set a flag in that file's CUSTOM box, not here.
# A key set here wins for `pnpm dev` and nothing else, so a stale value
# silently diverges this surface from the container — and an EMPTY assignment
# counts as a value, shadowing the generated one too. See [[env-files]]

# WARNING: Every NG_APP_* is compiled into the bundle — never put a secret in one.

# CONTRACT: Restart the dev server after changing any — they are inlined at
# BUILD time, so a browser reload re-serves the old value.

# The six the app reads; each one's CONTRACT lives in ../../.env.example.
# NG_APP_STRIPE_ENABLED=
# NG_APP_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# NG_APP_API_GATEWAY_URL=
# NG_APP_GEOCODE_ENABLED=
# NG_APP_WS_URL=
# NG_APP_RUM_ENABLED=
